<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/21st-century-bce">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Siege</p><h1 class="enc-title">Elamite sack of Ur</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 2004 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/21st-century-bce">21st century BCE</a> · Also known as sack of Ur</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Elamite sack of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ur">Ur</a> took place around 2004 BCE, when Elamite forces captured the city of Ur and took its last king, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ibbi-sin">Ibbi-Sin</a>, captive. It brought an end to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/neo-sumerian-empire">Neo-Sumerian Empire</a> and was later lamented in Sumerian literature.</p></div>
